$\because f(x)=\left|\begin{array}{ccc}\cos x & x & 1 \\ 2 \sin x & x & 2 x \\ \sin x & x & x\end{array}\right|\begin{array}{r}=\cos x\left(x^2-2 x^2\right)-x(2 x \sin x-2 x \sin x) \\ +1(2 x \sin x-x \sin x)\end{array}
$=-x^2 \cos x+x \sin x$
Now, $\lim _{x \rightarrow 0} \frac{f(x)}{x^2}=\lim _{x \rightarrow 0}\left(\frac{-x^2 \cos x+x \sin x}{x^2}\right)=\lim _{x \rightarrow 0}\left(-\cos x+\frac{\sin x}{x}\right)=-1+1 \quad\left[\because \lim _{x \rightarrow 0} \frac{\sin x}{x}=1\right]=0
